+.. _cli_inserting_data_convert:
+
+Transforming data before inserting it
+-------------------------------------
+
+Use ``--convert`` to execute Python code against each incoming object before it is inserted. The object is available to the code as ``row`` and can be modified in place. For example, this converts ``n`` to an integer and increments it::
+
+    $ cat rows.json \
+        | sqlite-utils insert data.db rows - --nl \
+            --convert 'row["n"] = int(row["n"]) + 1'
+
+Every input object is inserted after the conversion code has run. The code passed to this option is executed as Python, so only use code that you trust.
+
 .. _cli_inserting_data_flatten:
 
 Flattening nested JSON objects
